        "original_id": "0d9b63a1-8f88-544f-b4ab-1dee5561d878",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keitarō Urashima, Ken Akamatsu, Yūji Ueda, Derek Stephen Prince, Keitarō Arima, Urashima Tarō\n- Works: Love Hina, Digimon, Power Rangers Turbo, Power Rangers in Space\n- Roles: protagonist, voice actor, fictional character\n\nFacts:\n- Derek Stephen Prince was born on February 5, 1969, in Inglewood, California.\n- Derek Stephen Prince is an American voice actor known for roles in the Digimon series and for voicing Elgar in the live-action Power Rangers Turbo and Power Rangers in Space.\n- Keitarō Urashima is a fictional character and the protagonist of Ken Akamatsu's manga and anime Love Hina.\n- Yūji Ueda voices Keitarō Urashima in Japanese.\n- Derek Stephen Prince voices Keitarō Urashima in English.\n- Keitarō Urashima's name was inspired by Keitarō Arima and the mythological character Urashima Tarō.",
